{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793039945,"nonce":"WA9JiJvM6Opxchh+/riBU+5tGYY=","title":"Load runtime modules introduced by deferred macro expansions","message":"A focused Ashui component returning a switch of \u003cfor\u003e branches expands to new ashui.ui.For after Context.typeof has suspended the first macro pass. Without import ashui.ui.For, analysis reports expected Element, found Unknown at the switch; explicitly importing For removes that diagnostic. The tag still falls back to an expansion hover rather than the class in this focused probe.\n\nReproducer: a Component\u003c{}\u003e with @:build(ashui.ui.Markup.build()), imports of Element and Component, and pane(which:String):Element returning \u003cfor {n in [true]}\u003e\u003cdiv/\u003e\u003c/for\u003e in one switch case and a differently typed list in another. Use Ashui haxe and components/haxe class paths, tink_hxx and the HashLink target. The unchanged real Hxx implementation produces the correct final constructor text. Temporary protocol fixture: /tmp/rayzor-ashui-for-probe, logs /tmp/rayzor-ashui-for-release.log and /tmp/rayzor-ashui-for-explicit-import.log.\n\nCompilationUnit loads new qualified paths introduced by the early macro expansion pass. Investigate extending that dependency discovery to typer-dependent expansion results, preserving the real class identity and source-tag position. Do not infer a class from a hardcoded tag map.\n\nRelated: c07c045946b17db6b713f10010195b5be5451afa3b5e8ed76f07a27468bac713 and e27dcc980b6d4b7cd484dd0bcc6e35693fd1e7657dd4a40991ce29a72f4e8e3d.","files":null}]}